@Tetsurohhori thanks. Your 12b, run with our checker as data only (your verifier not opened), at `8ff69f4`: **agree**, `CHECKER_NOT_SIGNER` and nothing else (file sha256 `66f7b870…808f0`). Your SHA-1 vector also agrees under ours. So 12b plus 13–21 and our 22/23 give the same result from both verifiers, except 22, which waits on step 5.

To keep the numbers straight for @maximusrufus, we'd suggest:
- 12b replaces 12;
- our 23 (SHA-384 OID) is the algorithm pin, so your SHA-1 vector drops;
- our 22 (reference time = earlier of `issued_utc` and the covering token's genTime) lands only with the o

